-- title:
--   Two geometric components of the j-finite chart mod p
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N$ and $p$ with $N \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N$. Let $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ denote the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, and let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $p$ which is algebraically closed and carries a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra structure. Let $R =$ `chartAlgFin (N * p) p`, the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field of level $N p$ consisting of all elements integral over the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-subalgebra generated by the single element $j$ (the class `jFull` of the $j$-function); thus $R$ is the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j]$ in that function field. The assertion is that the set of minimal primes of the commutative ring $\kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} R$ — that is, the set of prime ideals minimal among those containing $(0)$ — is finite and has cardinality exactly $2$.
--
--   This is the statement that the geometric special fibre at $p$ of the cusp-free ($j$-finite) chart of the Igusa-type integral model at level $N p$, with $p \nmid N$, has exactly two irreducible components, the Deligne–Rapoport description of $X_0(Np)$ in characteristic $p$ as two copies of the level-$N$ curve glued along supersingular points. It feeds the later analysis of the fibres, residue fields and nodes of the model at Deligne–Rapoport level, and the identification of the relevant set of $j$-invariants at full level.
